@startuml TestCaptive Current Architecture
!theme plain
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho

title TestCaptive - Current Architecture (MVP)

package "Browser Layer" {
    component "Chrome Extension" as Chrome
    component "Content Script\n(Event Capture)" as ContentScript
    component "Background Script\n(Session Manager)" as BackgroundScript
    component "Web Application" as WebApp
    
    ContentScript -up-> Chrome
    BackgroundScript -up-> Chrome
    ContentScript --> WebApp : Monitors DOM\nCaptures Events
}

package "Development Environment" {
    component "VS Code Extension" as VSCode
    component "Review Panel\n(Webview UI)" as ReviewPanel
    component "Code Generator\n(Template Engine)" as CodeGen
    component "Test Data Manager\n(Session Storage)" as TestDataMgr
    
    ReviewPanel -up-> VSCode
    CodeGen -up-> VSCode
    TestDataMgr -up-> VSCode
}

package "Storage Layer" {
    database "Session Files\n(.json)" as SessionDB
}

package "Output Layer" {
    file "Playwright Test\n(.py)" as PlaywrightOutput
    file "Test Data\n(.json)" as TestDataOutput
}

' Workflow
WebApp --> [Content Script\n(Event Capture)] : User Actions
[Content Script\n(Event Capture)] --> [Background Script\n(Session Manager)] : Event Stream
[Background Script\n(Session Manager)] --> SessionDB : Save Session

SessionDB --> [Test Data Manager\n(Session Storage)] : Load Session
[Test Data Manager\n(Session Storage)] --> [Review Panel\n(Webview UI)] : Display Events
[Review Panel\n(Webview UI)] --> [Code Generator\n(Template Engine)] : Generate Code

[Code Generator\n(Template Engine)] --> PlaywrightOutput : Template Processing
[Test Data Manager\n(Session Storage)] --> TestDataOutput : Extract Data

note right of Chrome
  **Smart Event Capture**
  - Debouncing (500ms)
  - Deduplication
  - Element metadata
  - Session tracking
  - **Assertion capture** (7 types)
  - Context menu integration
end note

note right of [Code Generator\n(Template Engine)]
  **Multi-Pass Processing**
  - Conditional templates
  - Selector priority
  - Variable replacement
  - **Assertion generation**
  - Clean output
end note

note bottom of SessionDB
  **Session Data**
  - Events array
  - **Assertions array**
  - Element selectors
  - Input values
  - Timestamps
  - Page context
end note

@enduml
